                dcterms:relation "In 1979, the UNECE Convention on Long-range Transboundary Air Pollution, was signed to deal with air pollution on a broad regional basis. The Convention entered into force in 1983, laying down the general principles of international cooperation for air pollution abatement and setting up an institutional framework which has since brought together research and policy. WHO International Health Regulations (WHO, 2016)."@en ;
                dcterms:rights "Creative Commons CC BY 4.0" ;
                dcterms:source <https://www.preventionweb.net/hips-document/18c49b69d85b8e99> ,
                               <https://www.preventionweb.net/hips-document/6da9efd0e934eba8> ;
                dcterms:title "Air Pollution (Point Source)"@en ;
                xkos:causedBy hip-term:ch0202 ,
